**1. Wrong variable assigned — introduced functional bug. `src/Mod/Part/Gui/Command.cpp:1974`**
In `CmdPartRuledSurface::activated`, the replacement for the `subnames1` single-curve branch assigns to `curve2` where the old code assigned `curve1`:
```cpp
if (!subnames1.empty()) {
    curve2 = ...getTopoShape(docobj1, subnames1[0]...).getShape();   // was curve1
    link1 = subnames1[0];
}
```
The `link1`/`curve2` pairing is internally inconsistent, and the `subnames1.size() == 2` branch (line ~1981) overwrites `curve2` again. Net effect: `curve1` is never populated from the first object, so any 1-curve selection on the first object leaves the first ruling curve null → the command either fails or produces a degenerate ruled surface. This is the only converted call site in the PR where the assigned variable changed — almost certainly an editing slip. Fix: `curve1`.
